Researcher fix for FV8's released patch (NOT part of FV8). Opt-in: applied by
build-node-runtime.sh only with fv8 fixes "property-case", after
tools/fv8/patches/V8_patch_122.diff has been applied verbatim. Apply from
deps/v8 with: patch -p1 -F0 --forward

FV8's AstTraversal() (interpreter/bytecode-generator.cc) dispatches on numeric
AstNode::NodeType values. Its "Property" branch is labelled `case 44` and
calls pair.first->AsProperty(), but in V8 12.2 (both the authors' 12.2.281.21
and Node.js's 12.2.281.27, whose AST node lists are identical) 44 is
kOptionalChain and kProperty is 45. AsProperty() returns nullptr for any
non-Property node, so the branch dereferences a null pointer whenever FV8
traverses an untaken branch containing an optional chain (`a?.b`). The
authors' own comment on that line reads "case 45". This changes the label to
45 and nothing else; OptionalChain nodes then take the switch's default
branch, like every other node type FV8 does not handle.

--- a/src/interpreter/bytecode-generator.cc
+++ b/src/interpreter/bytecode-generator.cc
@@ -2118,7 +2118,7 @@
         break;
       }
       // FunctionLiteral
-      case 44: { // case 45: {
+      case 45: { // case 45: {
         auto node44 = static_cast<Property*>(pair.first->AsProperty());
         visited.push_back(pair.first);
 
